WATERMARK records:

W_MEMORY {
    memory_id
    event_id
    perspective_id
    observer
    source
    evidence_set
    observation
    interpretation
    determination
    uncertainty
    epoch
    jurisdiction
    provenance
}

Every memory statement can therefore answer:

> Who recorded this?



> When?



> Based on what evidence?



> What part is observation?



> What part is interpretation?



> Who determined its constitutional meaning?




---

X. ⚓ QUAY — IMMUTABLE MEMORY

QUAY preserves original records.

A later correction SHALL NOT destroy the earlier record.

Instead:

ORIGINAL RECORD
      ↓
CORRECTION
      ↓
RECONCILIATION

Thus:

CORRECTED
≠
ERASED

This establishes:

APPEND_ONLY_CONSTITUTIONAL_MEMORY


---

XI. 🏛️ MEMORY RECONCILIATION

R7.81 introduces:

MEMORY_RECONCILIATION

The reconciliation process:

RECORDS
 ↓
EVIDENCE NORMALIZATION
 ↓
SOURCE ANALYSIS
 ↓
TEMPORAL ALIGNMENT
 ↓
SEMANTIC COMPARISON
 ↓
CONTRADICTION ANALYSIS
 ↓
FOOL CHALLENGE
 ↓
TRIAS
 ↓
RECONCILIATION RESULT

Possible results:

RECONCILED
PARTIALLY_RECONCILED
MULTIPLE_VALID_PERSPECTIVES
CONTESTED
UNRESOLVED
INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE


---

XII. ⚖️ MULTIPLE VALID PERSPECTIVES

Two records may differ while both remain valid descriptions of different observations.

Example:

A observed:
"Authority was exercised."

B observed:
"Authority was not constitutionally recognized."

These are not necessarily contradictory.

They may represent:

OPERATIONAL FACT
vs
CONSTITUTIONAL STATUS

Therefore HORTUS must first determine whether claims are genuinely contradictory.


---

XIII. 🧮 CONTRADICTION CLASSES

R7.81 defines:

TYPE-I — APPARENT CONTRADICTION

Different wording, same underlying state.

A ≈ B

TYPE-II — PERSPECTIVE DIFFERENCE

Different observers report different dimensions.

A ≠ B
but
A ∧ B possible

TYPE-III — TEMPORAL DIFFERENCE

A(E₁)
B(E₂)

No contradiction if state legitimately changed.

TYPE-IV — TRUE CONFLICT

A ∧ ¬A

under identical:

subject
predicate
epoch
jurisdiction
conditions

TYPE-V — UNRESOLVED

Evidence is insufficient to determine whether contradiction exists.


---

XIV. 🔮 ORACLE — MEMORY DRIFT

ORACLE monitors:

MEMORY
 ↓
SOURCES
 ↓
INTERPRETATIONS
 ↓
DETERMINATIONS

and detects:

MEMORY_DRIFT
SOURCE_DRIFT
INTERPRETATION_DRIFT
RETROSPECTIVE_REWRITING
PROVENANCE_BREAK
EVIDENCE_DIVERGENCE
ARCHIVAL_MUTATION

Especially important:

RETROSPECTIVE_REWRITING

where the current state silently modifies the representation of the past.

ORACLE flags it.

TRIAS determines whether a correction is legitimate.


---

XV. 🛑 NO RETROACTIVE SILENT EDITING

R7.81 establishes:

PAST_RECORD
 ↓
NEW_EVIDENCE

must result in:

AMENDMENT
ANNOTATION
RECONCILIATION

not:

DELETE PAST
WRITE NEW PAST

Therefore:

THE FEDERATION MAY CORRECT ITS MEMORY, BUT SHALL NOT SECRETLY REWRITE IT.


