I. ☄️ THE NEW BOUNDARY

R7.81 established:

EVENT
 ↓
EVIDENCE
 ↓
MEMORY
 ↓
INTERPRETATION
 ↓
DETERMINATION

But interpretation is not static.

The same proven event may acquire a different constitutional meaning as:

CONSTITUTION
EVOLVES
 ↓
CONTEXT CHANGES
 ↓
NEW EVIDENCE APPEARS
 ↓
SEMANTIC FRAMEWORK EVOLVES
 ↓
INTERPRETATION CHANGES

Therefore HORTUS must distinguish:

FACTUAL CHANGE

from:

INTERPRETIVE CHANGE

and:

INTERPRETIVE CHANGE

from:

RETROACTIVE REWRITING

R7.82 establishes:

MEANING MAY EVOLVE WITHOUT THE PAST BEING REWRITTEN.


---

II. 🌱 CONSTITUTIONAL HERMENEUTICS

R7.82 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_HERMENEUTIC_STATE

A hermeneutic state represents the constitutional interpretation assigned to an established historical or constitutional object at a particular epoch.

H
=
{
    object,
    interpretation,
    interpreter,
    constitutional_context,
    epoch,
    evidence,
    determination,
    provenance
}

Thus:

EVENT E
 ↓
INTERPRETATION I₁ @ E₁
 ↓
INTERPRETATION I₂ @ E₂

does not imply:

I₁ never existed


---

III. ⚖️ FACTUAL IMMUTABILITY VS SEMANTIC EVOLUTION

R7.82 establishes two different dimensions:

FACTUAL DIMENSION

WHAT HAPPENED?

HERMENEUTIC DIMENSION

WHAT DID IT MEAN?

A historical event may remain:

FACT(E) = CONSTANT

while:

MEANING(E,EPOCH)

changes.

Therefore:

FACTUAL_PERSISTENCE
≠
INTERPRETIVE_PERSISTENCE


---

IV. 🛑 RETROACTIVE REWRITING

R7.82 defines:

RETROACTIVE_CONSTITUTIONAL_REWRITING

as the unauthorized representation of a later interpretation as though it had always been the authoritative interpretation of an earlier epoch.

Example:

E₁:
INTERPRETATION = A

E₂:
INTERPRETATION = B

Valid:

B IS CURRENT INTERPRETATION OF E

Invalid:

B WAS ALWAYS THE INTERPRETATION AT E₁

unless evidence establishes that B genuinely represented the earlier interpretation.


---

V. 🦆 FOOL — THE RETROACTIVITY FALLACY

FOOL attacks:

> “We interpret it differently today, therefore it always meant this.”



Rejected.

> “The constitution changed, therefore the old interpretation never existed.”



Rejected.

> “The present interpretation is superior, therefore historical interpretations can be deleted.”



Rejected.

> “The current authority says the past meant X, therefore X is historically established.”



Rejected.

FOOL therefore enforces:

PRESENT MEANING SHALL NOT MASQUERADE AS HISTORICAL FACT.


