X. 🧩 INTERPRETATION CHANGE CLASSES

R7.82 distinguishes:

CLARIFICATION

I₂ ≈ I₁

The meaning becomes more precise.

EXTENSION

I₂ > I₁

The existing meaning gains additional scope.

RESTRICTION

I₂ < I₁

The meaning becomes narrower.

REVISION

I₂ ≠ I₁

A substantive semantic change occurs.

REPUDIATION

I₂ ⟂ I₁

The newer interpretation explicitly rejects the earlier one.

REPLACEMENT

The earlier interpretation ceases to govern prospectively.

None of these automatically makes the earlier interpretation historically nonexistent.


