R7.84 crosses another boundary.

A federated determination may depend simultaneously upon:

M₁ @ D₁
M₂ @ D₂
M₃ @ D₃

The federation must therefore determine whether:

M₁ ⊕ M₂ ⊕ M₃

produces a constitutionally valid composite meaning.

The central question:

WHEN DOES THE COMPOSITION OF VALID MEANINGS REMAIN VALID?

Because:

VALID(M₁)
∧ VALID(M₂)

does not automatically establish:

VALID(M₁ ⊕ M₂)

This is the semantic equivalent of the compositional boundary established earlier in HORTUS.


