P proves that P's validation of itself is valid
      ↓
?

The constitutional question is therefore:

CAN A PROOF VALIDATE THE CONDITIONS THAT MAKE THAT SAME PROOF VALID WITHOUT CREATING A CIRCULAR CERTIFICATION LOOP?

R7.86 answers:

> Self-reference SHALL be representable, but self-validation SHALL NOT be accepted merely because the reference closes.




---

II. 🌱 META-PROOF

R7.86 introduces:

META_PROOF

A meta-proof is evidence establishing a property of another proof, certificate, validation procedure, or proof domain.

P₁
 ↓
proves
 ↓
property(P₂)

Examples:

P₁ → P₂_VALID
P₁ → DOMAIN(P₂)_SOUND
P₁ → CERTIFICATE(P₂)_VALID
P₁ → REPLAY(P₂)_CORRECT

But:

P₁ → P₁_VALID

is not automatically sufficient.


---

III. 🧬 PROOF LEVELS

HORTUS establishes explicit levels:

L0  STATE
 ↓
L1  PROOF OF STATE
 ↓
L2  PROOF OF PROOF
 ↓
L3  PROOF OF PROOF SYSTEM
 ↓
L4  PROOF OF META-PROOF SYSTEM

The level itself becomes attributable.

A proof at L2 cannot silently acquire L3 authority.

Therefore:

META-LEVEL ESCALATION REQUIRES EXPLICIT VALIDATION.


---

IV. ⚖️ REFLEXIVE VALIDATION

R7.86 introduces:

REFLEXIVE_VALIDATION

A system is reflexive when it reasons about properties of its own:

proofs

certificates

domains

rules

validators

evidence

semantic interpretations


Reflexivity is not itself invalid.

The danger lies in:

VALIDATOR V
   ↓
validates
   ↓
V

without an independent grounding condition.


---

V. 🛑 CIRCULAR CERTIFICATION

R7.86 defines:

CERTIFICATION_CYCLE

Example:

P₁ proves C₁
C₁ validates P₂
P₂ validates C₂
C₂ validates P₁

This creates:

P₁ → C₁ → P₂ → C₂ → P₁

A cycle is not automatically invalid.

But it cannot establish foundational validity merely from itself.

Therefore:

CYCLE
≠
PROOF

unless the cycle has an independently grounded invariant or base proof.


---

VI. 🦆 FOOL — CIRCULARITY ATTACK

FOOL attacks:

> “Certificate A validates B and B validates A, therefore both are valid.”



Rejected.

> “The validator says the validator is correct.”



Rejected without independent basis.

> “The proof system successfully replayed itself once, therefore it is sound.”



Rejected.

> “No contradiction has been observed in the validation loop.”



Rejected.

FOOL therefore introduces:

CIRCULARITY_CHALLENGE

which asks:

WHERE IS THE EXTERNAL OR LOWER-LEVEL GROUND?


---

