VIII. 🔐 ANTI-CIRCULARITY ROOT

R7.86 introduces:

PROOF_GROUND

A proof ground is a constitutionally accepted basis that does not depend on the proposition currently being validated.

Conceptually:

G
 ↓
P₁
 ↓
C₁
 ↓
P₂

where G provides the independent grounding relation.

Without such a ground:

P₁ → C₁ → P₂ → C₂ → P₁

remains circular.

The system must therefore be able to answer:

> Where does the validity chain bottom out?




