II. 🌱 CONSTITUTIONAL IDENTITY

R7.87 introduces:

CONSTITUTIONAL_IDENTITY

A constitutional identity is the set of properties that must remain invariant for an evolved system to be recognized as constitutionally continuous with its predecessor.

Conceptually:

C₁
 ↓ EVOLUTION
C₂

does not imply:

IDENTITY(C₁,C₂)

Identity requires an explicit determination.


