XXXI. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O691

A constitutionally valid anchor SHALL NOT become invalid merely because another valid anchor exists.

CIP-O692

Reference validity SHALL remain distinguishable from reference compatibility.

CIP-O693

Multiple valid anchors SHALL NOT automatically establish multiple constitutional authorities.

CIP-O694

Anchor conflict SHALL require demonstrable constitutional overlap.

CIP-O695

Difference between anchors SHALL NOT automatically constitute constitutional conflict.

CIP-O696

Reference partitioning SHALL require explicit domain-boundary proof.

CIP-O697

Reference partitioning SHALL NOT be used to conceal constitutional conflict.

CIP-O698

Common constitutional core SHALL NOT automatically become a new anchor.

CIP-O699

Reconciliation SHALL preserve participating anchor lineage.

CIP-O700

Reconciliation SHALL NOT erase constitutional plurality.

CIP-O701

FOOL SHALL challenge manufactured reference plurality.

CIP-O702

BRAINPOWER SHALL model relationships between constitutional reference frames.

CIP-O703

ORACLE SHALL monitor reference fragmentation and anchor constellation instability.

CIP-O704

TRIAS SHALL determine constitutional compatibility and reconciliation.

CIP-O705

WATERMARK SHALL preserve multi-anchor reconciliation provenance.

CIP-O706

QUAY SHALL preserve immutable anchor constellation lineage.

CIP-O707

R5 SHALL replay multi-anchor reconciliation determinations.

CIP-O708

Local anchor validity SHALL NOT imply federated reference validity.

CIP-O709

Federated composition SHALL NOT inherit a reference frame implicitly.

CIP-O710

Federated reference selection SHALL be explicit and evidence-bound.

CIP-O711

Anchor shopping SHALL NOT constitute constitutional reference selection.

CIP-O712

Reference selection SHALL NOT be determined after substantive decision solely to justify that decision.

CIP-O713

A valid anchor SHALL NOT inherit authority merely through federation membership.

CIP-O714

A reference conflict SHALL NOT be resolved by majority preference alone.

CIP-O715

A constitutional singularity SHALL be independently proven.

CIP-O716

Unresolved reference conflict SHALL NOT silently become execution authority.

CIP-O717

Reference plurality SHALL remain historically traceable.

CIP-O718

Partitioned reference domains SHALL preserve cross-domain boundary provenance.

CIP-O719

A reconciliation certificate SHALL identify all participating anchors relevant to its proof domain.

CIP-O720

A constitutionally unproven common reference SHALL NOT be used for federated proof inheritance.


