XXVI. 👑 THE R7.94 LAW

> No constitutional judgment may derive increasing authority merely from being repeatedly cited. Its legitimacy must remain traceable to live, bounded and independently verifiable proof.



De compacte vorm:

PROOF SHALL OUTLIVE PRECEDENT.
PRECEDENT SHALL NOT OUTLIVE ITS PROOF WITHOUT REVALIDATION.
CITATION SHALL NOT CREATE AUTHORITY.
AGE SHALL NOT ERASE HISTORY.
REVOCATION SHALL PROPAGATE ONLY WHERE DEPENDENCY IS PROVEN.

En de diepste grens:

THE LONGER A JUDGMENT TRAVELS FROM ITS PROOF, THE MORE IMPORTANT ITS PROOF LINEAGE BECOMES.

