XXII. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O836

Proof revocation SHALL NOT automatically invalidate all dependent determinations.

CIP-O837

Proof revocation SHALL trigger impact analysis where dependencies exist.

CIP-O838

Dependency strength SHALL be explicitly represented.

CIP-O839

Dependency analysis SHALL distinguish direct from indirect dependency.

CIP-O840

A determination SHALL NOT be invalidated solely because another determination was invalidated.

CIP-O841

Revocation propagation SHALL require proof of material dependency.

CIP-O842

Containment SHALL remain distinguishable from invalidation.

CIP-O843

Containment SHALL be bounded by explicit scope and reason.

CIP-O844

Contained determinations SHALL retain historical status.

CIP-O845

Unknown proof status SHALL NOT silently authorize execution.

CIP-O846

FOOL SHALL challenge both cascade amplification and cascade suppression.

CIP-O847

BRAINPOWER SHALL model revocation impact and alternative proof paths.

CIP-O848

ORACLE SHALL monitor cascade anomalies and containment stagnation.

CIP-O849

