CIP-O851

QUAY SHALL preserve immutable revocation and recovery history.

CIP-O852

R5 SHALL replay proof revocation and dependency cascades.

CIP-O853

Revalidation SHALL be independently provable.

CIP-O854

Recovery SHALL NOT erase the historical revoked proof.

CIP-O855

Proof succession SHALL remain distinguishable from proof replacement.

CIP-O856

A successor proof SHALL identify preserved and changed claims.

CIP-O857

Recovery SHALL NOT silently alter constitutional identity.

CIP-O858

Local proof revocation SHALL NOT automatically invalidate federated determinations.

CIP-O859

Federated revocation impact SHALL require federated dependency analysis.

CIP-O860

Containment SHALL NOT become indefinite constitutional limbo without review.

CIP-O861

Revalidation SHALL terminate in an explicit determination.

CIP-O862

Alternative proof SHALL be independently validated before restoring reliance.

CIP-O863

Revocation SHALL remain historically traceable.

CIP-O864

Cascade breadth SHALL not itself establish constitutional significance.

CIP-O865

Cascade depth SHALL not itself establish constitutional invalidity.


