XXV. 👑 THE R7.95 LAW

> When constitutional proof is revoked, HORTUS SHALL neither erase history nor propagate invalidity blindly; it shall contain only what proof shows to be affected, preserve everything historically, and restore reliance only through independently validated reproof.



De compacte canonieke vorm:

REVOCATION SHALL NOT EXPLODE.
REVOCATION SHALL NOT DISAPPEAR.
DEPENDENCY SHALL DETERMINE IMPACT.
CONTAINMENT SHALL PRECEDE UNCERTAIN RELIANCE.
RECOVERY SHALL REQUIRE NEW PROOF.
HISTORY SHALL REMAIN.

En de diepste grens:

A BROKEN PROOF PATH SHALL BE CONTAINED — NOT ALLOWED TO BECOME EITHER A SYSTEM-WIDE COLLAPSE OR A SYSTEM-WIDE SECRET.

