XXIII. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O956

A constitutional determination SHALL identify its materially relevant context.

CIP-O957

Rule identity SHALL remain distinguishable from contextual state.

CIP-O958

Semantic identity SHALL remain distinguishable from contextual equivalence.

CIP-O959

Different contextual outcomes SHALL NOT by themselves establish constitutional inconsistency.

CIP-O960

Material context SHALL remain provenance-bearing.

CIP-O961

Context SHALL remain epoch-bound.

CIP-O962

Historical context SHALL NOT be retroactively rewritten.

CIP-O963

QUAY SHALL preserve immutable contextual history.

CIP-O964

WATERMARK SHALL preserve contextual provenance.

CIP-O965

R5 SHALL replay materially relevant historical context.

CIP-O966

FOOL SHALL challenge contextual omission and manipulation.

CIP-O967

BRAINPOWER SHALL model constitutional context space.

CIP-O968

ORACLE SHALL monitor contextual drift and anomaly.

CIP-O969

TRIAS SHALL determine contextual constitutional validity.

CIP-O970

A determination SHALL NOT silently depend upon hidden context.

CIP-O971

Material context completeness SHALL be independently verifiable.

CIP-O972

Context fields SHALL remain attributable to their applicable authority.

CIP-O973

Context authority SHALL remain distinguishable from execution authority.

CIP-O974

Context authority SHALL remain distinguishable from proof authority.

CIP-O975

Context authority SHALL remain distinguishable from reference authority.

CIP-O976

Federated context comparison SHALL remain distinct from local context validation.

CIP-O977

Local contextual validity SHALL NOT automatically establish federated contextual validity.

CIP-O978

Contextual difference SHALL be evaluated by constitutional effect, not field count alone.

CIP-O979

Counterfactual context replay SHALL preserve historical rule and semantic state.

CIP-O980

A context snapshot SHALL remain immutable once used as evidentiary input.


