XXIV. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O1081

A constitutional reconciliation SHALL NOT automatically establish a new constitution.

CIP-O1082

A settlement SHALL remain distinguishable from a constitutional foundation.

CIP-O1083

Reconciliation authority SHALL remain explicitly bounded.

CIP-O1084

Settlement authority SHALL remain distinguishable from execution authority.

CIP-O1085

A reconciliation SHALL NOT automatically increase constitutional authority.

CIP-O1086

A reconciliation SHALL preserve material input lineage.

CIP-O1087

A reconciliation SHALL preserve material conflict provenance.

CIP-O1088

QUAY SHALL preserve all material pre-reconciliation states.

CIP-O1089

WATERMARK SHALL preserve reconciliation provenance.

CIP-O1090

R5 SHALL replay material reconciliation chains.

CIP-O1091

FOOL SHALL challenge post-reconciliation authority escalation.

CIP-O1092

ORACLE SHALL monitor post-reconciliation authority growth.

CIP-O1093

BRAINPOWER SHALL model reconciliation lineage and authority inheritance.

CIP-O1094

TRIAS SHALL determine reconciliation validity.

CIP-O1095

A settlement SHALL remain bounded by its explicit jurisdiction.

CIP-O1096

A settlement SHALL remain bounded by its explicit temporal epoch.

CIP-O1097

A settlement SHALL remain bounded by its explicit composition domain.

CIP-O1098

Settlement scope expansion SHALL require explicit revalidation.

CIP-O1099

A settlement SHALL NOT silently become a universal reference.

CIP-O1100

A federated settlement SHALL NOT automatically become a federated root.

CIP-O1101

Reconciliation chains SHALL remain traceable to their participating roots.

CIP-O1102

Reconciliation depth SHALL remain observable.

CIP-O1103

Repeated reconciliation SHALL NOT itself establish authority.

CIP-O1104

Post-reconciliation drift SHALL remain separately measurable.

CIP-O1105

Origin drift SHALL remain traceable through reconciliation.

CIP-O1106

Merge drift SHALL NOT erase predecessor drift.

CIP-O1107

A settlement output SHALL NOT become its own sole legitimacy proof.

CIP-O1108

A settlement SHALL NOT authorize itself.

CIP-O1109

A reconciliation rule SHALL remain independently identifiable.

CIP-O1110

Material assumptions used in reconciliation SHALL remain recorded.

CIP-O1111

Changed properties SHALL remain distinguishable from preserved invariants.

CIP-O1112

Unresolved conflicts SHALL remain visible after settlement.

CIP-O1113

A settlement SHALL NOT retroactively alter participating root validity.

CIP-O1114

A settlement SHALL NOT retroactively alter historical constitutional meaning.

CIP-O1115

Reference promotion after reconciliation SHALL require explicit constitutional determination.

CIP-O1116

Authority inherited through reconciliation SHALL be limited to explicitly proven authority.

CIP-O1117

Reconciliation composition SHALL remain independently replayable.

CIP-O1118

Loss of reconciliation lineage SHALL trigger revalidation.

CIP-O1119

Material post-reconciliation authority expansion SHALL trigger review.

CIP-O1120

No reconciliation SHALL convert constitutional complexity into untraceable authority.


