XVII. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O1171

An interpretive conflict SHALL remain explicitly identifiable.

CIP-O1172

Competing material interpretations SHALL remain provenance-bound.

CIP-O1173

Interpretive contestation SHALL precede material adjudication where contestation is available.

CIP-O1174

Adjudicative authority SHALL remain explicitly bounded.

CIP-O1175

An adjudicator SHALL NOT derive authority solely from its own determination.

CIP-O1176

A determination SHALL NOT automatically constitute constitutional truth.

CIP-O1177

A determination SHALL NOT automatically become universal precedent.

CIP-O1178

Reference promotion SHALL require explicit determination.

CIP-O1179

Alternative material interpretations SHALL remain historically traceable.

CIP-O1180

Dissenting positions SHALL remain preserved where materially relevant.

CIP-O1181

FOOL SHALL retain the ability to challenge adjudicative reasoning.

CIP-O1182

ORACLE SHALL monitor adjudicative concentration.

CIP-O1183

BRAINPOWER SHALL model determination dependency.

CIP-O1184

TRIAS SHALL remain bounded by its explicit adjudicative authority.

CIP-O1185

WATERMARK SHALL preserve adjudication provenance.

CIP-O1186

QUAY SHALL preserve pre-adjudication conflict states.

CIP-O1187

R5 SHALL replay material adjudication chains.

CIP-O1188

A determination SHALL remain bounded by jurisdiction.

CIP-O1189

A determination SHALL remain bounded by temporal epoch.

CIP-O1190

A determination SHALL remain bounded by semantic scope.

CIP-O1191

A later determination SHALL NOT erase the historical existence of an earlier determination.

CIP-O1192

Repeated citation SHALL NOT itself establish constitutional supremacy.

CIP-O1193

Precedent accumulation SHALL remain observable.

CIP-O1194

Adjudication centralization SHALL remain observable.

CIP-O1195

Material new evidence SHALL be capable of triggering review.

CIP-O1196

Adjudication SHALL remain distinguishable from amendment.

CIP-O1197

Adjudication SHALL remain distinguishable from execution.

CIP-O1198

Adjudication SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutional foundation.

CIP-O1199

Interpretive conflict resolution SHALL NOT erase semantic plurality.

CIP-O1200

No adjudicative process SHALL convert procedural authority into unbounded constitutional sovereignty.


