XVIII. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O1251

A constitutionally valid possibility SHALL remain distinguishable from an actual state.

CIP-O1252

Counterfactual evidence SHALL NOT be treated as evidence of actuality.

CIP-O1253

Actuality SHALL NOT retroactively establish inevitability.

CIP-O1254

Material valid alternative paths SHALL remain provenance-traceable.

CIP-O1255

QUAY SHALL preserve material constitutional possibilities.

CIP-O1256

WATERMARK SHALL preserve possibility provenance.

CIP-O1257

BRAINPOWER SHALL distinguish actual, possible, rejected and expired paths.

CIP-O1258

FOOL SHALL challenge counterfactual erasure and actuality confusion.

CIP-O1259

ORACLE SHALL monitor possibility-memory degradation.

CIP-O1260

TRIAS SHALL determine possibility validity within explicit scope.

CIP-O1261

A valid possibility SHALL NOT automatically acquire authority.

CIP-O1262

Repeated reference to a possibility SHALL NOT establish constitutional validity.

CIP-O1263

A rejected possibility SHALL remain historically distinguishable from a possibility that never existed.

CIP-O1264

An expired possibility SHALL remain historically traceable.

CIP-O1265

Possibility expiry SHALL NOT retroactively alter origin validity.

CIP-O1266

Opportunity loss SHALL remain observable.

CIP-O1267

Irreversible path transitions SHALL record material opportunity loss.

CIP-O1268

Possibility status changes SHALL NOT rewrite historical provenance.

CIP-O1269

A counterfactual record SHALL remain explicitly labeled as counterfactual.

CIP-O1270

No constitutional possibility SHALL become a constitutional fact solely through persistence in memory.


