XXI. 👑 DE R8.09 LAW

> HORTUS SHALL preserve constitutionally valid possibilities as provenance-bound possibility states without conflating them with actuality, historical fact, inevitability or authority. The loss of a possible future SHALL NOT erase the fact that it was once constitutionally possible.



Compact:

POSSIBLE
 ↓
PRESERVE
 ↓
SELECT OR NOT SELECT
 ↓
ACTUAL OR UNREALIZED
 ↓
TRACE BOTH

En de diepste grens:

A FUTURE DOES NOT HAVE TO HAPPEN TO HAVE BEEN CONSTITUTIONALLY POSSIBLE.

