XIX. ☄️ CANONICAL INVARIANTS

CIP-O1331

Legitimate constitutional determinations MAY coexist.

CIP-O1332

Disagreement SHALL NOT automatically constitute invalidity.

CIP-O1333

Consensus SHALL NOT automatically constitute constitutional authority.

CIP-O1334

Majority size SHALL NOT automatically determine constitutional validity.

CIP-O1335

Minority determinations SHALL remain provenance-traceable.

CIP-O1336

Material disagreement SHALL remain explicitly recorded.

CIP-O1337

WATERMARK SHALL preserve determination plurality.

CIP-O1338

QUAY SHALL preserve historical disagreement records.

CIP-O1339

BRAINPOWER SHALL model determination relationships.

CIP-O1340

FOOL SHALL challenge consensus supremacy.

CIP-O1341

ORACLE SHALL monitor dissent suppression.

CIP-O1342

TRIAS SHALL determine valid coexistence.

CIP-O1343

Consensus SHALL remain distinguishable from evidence.

CIP-O1344

Consensus SHALL remain distinguishable from authority.

CIP-O1345

A determination SHALL NOT establish its own legitimacy through circular agreement.

CIP-O1346

Independent determinations SHALL preserve independent provenance.

CIP-O1347

Jurisdictional differences SHALL remain explicit.

CIP-O1348

Interpretive differences SHALL remain explicit.

CIP-O1349

Threshold differences SHALL remain explicit.

CIP-O1350

Material disagreement SHALL NOT be erased by later resolution.

CIP-O1351

Resolution SHALL produce a new attributable determination.

CIP-O1352

Historical dissent SHALL remain historically visible.

CIP-O1353

A resolved disagreement SHALL remain distinguishable from an absent disagreement.

CIP-O1354

Repeated agreement SHALL NOT independently create authority.

CIP-O1355

Epistemic diversity SHALL remain analytically observable.

CIP-O1356

Plural determinations SHALL remain bounded by their applicable scope.

CIP-O1357

No determination SHALL become universally authoritative solely through consensus.

CIP-O1358

Disagreement SHALL remain distinguishable from contradiction.

CIP-O1359

Contradiction SHALL remain distinguishable from invalidity.

CIP-O1360

Constitutional pluralism SHALL NOT become constitutional relativism.


