> A constitutional system SHALL remain capable of distinguishing adaptive state transformation from constitutional identity transformation. Recursive evolution SHALL NOT by itself establish continuity of constitutional identity. Material changes to constitutional roots, authority boundaries, jurisdiction, rules, proof requirements, or other identity-defining invariants SHALL remain detectable, attributable, externally anchorable where required, and subject to revalidation.



