> A constitutional system SHALL distinguish possible futures, predicted futures, preferred futures, selected futures, and constitutionally authorized futures. No future SHALL acquire constitutional status solely through probability, convergence, repetition, system preference, prediction, self-reinforcing selection, or claims of inevitability. Material future selection SHALL remain attributable, provenance-preserved, authority-bounded, jurisdiction-aware, externally anchorable where required, and independently revalidatable.



