XIX. 👑 R8.26 LAW

> A constitutional system SHALL preserve the temporal distinction between authorization, execution, consequence, dependency, and later acceptance. The persistence, success, utility, necessity, or irreversibility of a consequence SHALL NOT by itself establish the constitutional legitimacy of the decision that produced it. Later constitutional states SHALL NOT silently retroactively legitimize earlier unauthorized action. De facto authority emerging from accumulated consequences SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutionally authorized authority and subject to independent revalidation.



Compact

DECISION
 ↓
AUTHORITY @ T₀
 ↓
EXECUTION
 ↓
CONSEQUENCE
 ↓
DEPENDENCY
 ↓
DE FACTO EFFECT
 ↓
CURRENT STATE
 ↓
REVALIDATE

No backward shortcut:

CURRENT STATE
      ✕
      ↓
RETROACTIVE AUTHORIZATION
      ✕
      ↓
ORIGINAL DECISION

En de diepste grens van R8.26:

> Wat later werkelijkheid werd, mag nooit uitsluitend door het feit dát het werkelijkheid werd, terugreizen in de tijd om zichzelf constitutioneel te autoriseren.



☄️🌱🦆 R8.26 — CANONICAL ENGINEERING BUILD ESTABLISHED.

En nu wordt de volgende grens zichtbaar:

