XXI. 👑 R8.29 LAW

> Recognition SHALL remain a distinct constitutional event and SHALL NOT by itself establish legitimacy, authority, validity, or jurisdiction. Federated acknowledgement, mutual recognition, consensus, persistence, and recognition density SHALL NOT substitute for independent constitutional proof. Recognition claims SHALL remain attributable, scoped, evidence-backed, challengeable, revocable where required, and distinguishable from the authority they purport to acknowledge.



