XXIII. 👑 R8.32 LAW

> Emergent behaviour SHALL remain distinguishable from constitutional authorization. Persistent patterns, structural dependencies, de facto rules, emergent jurisdiction, and authority accretion SHALL remain observable, attributable, challengeable, and subject to constitutional classification where their effects become material. No system SHALL acquire constitutional authority solely through repetition, convergence, dependency, persistence, or emergent coordination.



