XX. 👑 R8.37 LAW

> A constitutional system SHALL treat persistent, emergent patterns as constitutionally relevant when they materially affect authority, jurisdiction, access, procedure, evidence, alternatives, or other governance structures, even where no actor explicitly designed or authorized the pattern. Emergence SHALL remain distinguishable from legitimacy, persistence SHALL NOT constitute authorization, and no emergent structure SHALL acquire constitutional authority solely through repetition, convergence, dependency, or system-wide acceptance.



