XIX. 🜂🔥 R8.45 LAW

> A constitutional system SHALL distinguish repeated behavior, custom, emergent norm, institutional practice, formal rule, and constitutional rule. No normative structure SHALL acquire constitutional authority solely through repetition, persistence, social expectation, convergence, institutionalization, or self-reinforcement. The origin, provenance, dissent, authority claim, and constitutional status of emergent norms SHALL remain independently observable and revalidatable.



