Not every emergent structure deserves constitutional escalation.

R8.57 therefore introduces:

STRUCTURAL_MATERIALITY

A pattern becomes materially significant where it demonstrably affects one or more of:

authority

jurisdiction

identity

access

decision pathways

resource allocation

role assignment

dependency

alternative availability

constitutional outcomes


Thus:

STRUCTURE
   +
MATERIAL_EFFECT
   ↓
REVIEW CANDIDATE

Not:

STRUCTURE
   ↓
AUTHORITY


---

III. ⚖️ THE FIVE-GATE MODEL

Every candidate emergent structure passes through five independent gates:

G1 — EXISTENCE

Does the structure actually exist?

Evidence:

events
interactions
repetition
temporal persistence

G2 — STRUCTURALITY

Has recurrence become a system-level relationship rather than isolated behavior?

G3 — MATERIALITY

Does the structure materially change system possibilities or outcomes?

G4 — PROVENANCE

Can its formation be reconstructed?

G5 — CONSTITUTIONAL SIGNIFICANCE

Does the structure affect a constitutionally protected domain?

Only then:

TRIAS REVIEW

And even then:

TRIAS REVIEW
   ≠
AUTHORIZATION


