XVII. 🜂 R8.57 LAW

> An emergent structure becomes constitutionally reviewable when persistent interaction produces a demonstrable material effect upon authority, jurisdiction, identity, decision paths, alternatives or constitutional outcomes. Such reviewability SHALL NOT itself constitute legitimacy or authorization. The emergence, materiality, provenance, reversibility and constitutional effects of the structure SHALL remain independently observable and challengeable.



