R8.59 takes the next necessary step:

> What happens when an emergent structure has become materially harmful, entrenched, and constitutionally significant?



The answer cannot simply be “delete it.”

A constitutionally embedded structure may carry dependencies, identities, histories, relationships and operational state. Abrupt removal can itself create constitutional damage.

