 ↓
B'
 ↓
A₁

Where:

A₀ ≠ A₁

because history changed:

dependencies,

expectations,

authority,

information,

relationships,

available alternatives.


This is constitutional hysteresis.


---

III. 🧬 RESTORATION ≠ RESET

R8.65 establishes:

RECOVERY
   ≠
RESET

and:

ROLLBACK
   ≠
RESTORATION

A technical rollback may restore bytes.

It does not necessarily restore:

human expectations,

relational structures,

accumulated authority,

learned system behavior,

dependency,

institutional memory.


Therefore:

> Constitutional restoration SHALL be evaluated at the structural level, not merely at the state-representation level.




