R8.68 established Epistemic Feedback.

The next boundary is unavoidable:

> If a system observes an outcome, how does it know what actually caused it?



Because an outcome can be attributed incorrectly.

A system may say:

DECISION A
 ↓
OUTCOME B

and conclude:

> “A caused B.”



But perhaps:

A + BIAS + CONTEXT + EXTERNAL EVENT + PRIOR STRUCTURE
                         ↓
                       OUTCOME

The system may then use the incorrectly attributed outcome to strengthen the authority of A.

That creates:

CAUSAL_LEGITIMACY_ERROR

And the deeper mechanism:

SELF_ATTRIBUTED_AUTHORITY


