Before an outcome can materially strengthen a constitutional claim, the system must distinguish:

temporal sequence,

causal dependency,

confounding,

feedback,

external causes,

counterfactual alternatives.



---

III. ⚠️ THE COUNTERFACTUAL TEST

A powerful question enters the canon:

> What would have happened if the decision had not occurred?



Conceptually:

WORLD A
DECISION
 ↓
OUTCOME

WORLD B
NO DECISION
 ↓
?

If the difference cannot be meaningfully established, causal confidence must remain bounded.

Thus:

> Observed succession SHALL NOT be treated as sufficient proof of causal necessity.




