XIX. 🜂 R8.73 LAW

> Where system responses to an actor's exercise of agency materially alter that actor's future options, capabilities, relationships or decision conditions, the resulting feedback SHALL remain observable, attributable and historically reconstructable. System-generated conditioning SHALL NOT be treated as independent proof of the preference, necessity or authority that the conditioning itself helped produce.



Compact

ACTOR
 ↓
AGENCY
 ↓
